# User Profile — per-developer (TEMPLATE)

This is the **committed template**. Every developer on the project starts from the same file, then
keeps their own filled-in copy **locally** — `.agents/memory/user-profile.md` is gitignored, so your
notes about how *you* work never land in someone else's checkout.

**First-time setup (run once after cloning):**

```bash
cp .agents/memory/user-profile.md.example .agents/memory/user-profile.md
```

Then fill in the sections below in your copy and flip the frontmatter to `status: populated`.
Until it says `populated`, every command that would load it skips it (CLAUDE.md → Automatic Behaviors),
so an unfilled profile costs nothing.

> Solo project? Same flow — the copy just happens to be the only one.

